{
  "$comment": "Per-suite wall-clock durations (ms) for the general-server vitest lane, used by scripts/general-server-shard.mjs to balance suites across the PR shard matrix. Sampled from a real PR run of .github/workflows/pr.yml (actions run 34533751794, 2026-09-10, scratch diagnostic PR misterbusiness1/paperclip#95 off PR #93 head 828bb1193428c93cc0f2d58d325dbab402cc42cb, timeout-minutes temporarily raised so every shard could finish) by diffing consecutive per-suite completion timestamps in the general-server portion of the 'Run grouped general test suites' log -- that captures each suite's true serial cost (import + collect + tests), not just the vitest-reported test time. Refreshes the prior 2026-08-04 snapshot (279/421 files) with full coverage of all 324 files the general-server group currently owns (OXFA-31270 -- the earlier snapshot silently median-weighted 142 files added since). Suites missing here get the median weight, so the manifest only needs occasional refreshes. Upgrade merge of upstream v2026.831.1: entries for suites the fork snapshot does not cover were taken from upstream's 2026-08-24 manifest (actions run 32708351172); fork-measured values win where both exist, and entries for suites that no longer exist were dropped. Upgrade merge of upstream v2026.916.1: same rule again -- fork-measured values win, upstream's 2026-09-09/09-11 manifest supplies suites the fork snapshot does not cover (including the heavy chat-channels.integration and native-codex-runner.integration suites, see $chatSample/$nativeRunnerSample), and entries for suites that no longer exist were dropped.",
